# Payload Blocks & Collections

Reference the Payload skill at `.claude/skills/payload/SKILL.md` for the canonical patterns. This rule pins project-specific conventions on top.

## Block file structure

For each block:

```
src/blocks/<BlockName>/
├── config.ts        ← Payload Block config, default export NOT used
└── Component.tsx    ← React renderer accepting block props from Page['layout'][N]
```

- The block `slug` is camelCase (`'offerShowcase'`); `interfaceName` is PascalCase (`'OfferShowcaseBlock'`).
- Register the block in `src/collections/Pages/index.ts` under `layout.blocks`, then add the component to `blockComponents` in `src/blocks/RenderBlocks.tsx`.
- Run `pnpm payload generate:types` after schema changes; commit the updated `src/payload-types.ts`.

## Field conventions

- Use `slugField()` from Payload for unique URL slugs (do not handroll).
- For links, always use the project's `linkGroup` factory in `src/fields/linkGroup.ts`; never re-implement Link UI per block.
- Media uploads use `relationTo: 'media'`, never raw URL strings.
- Rich text uses the standard `lexicalEditor` config matching `Content` / `CallToAction` blocks — keep the same toolbar features unless the design demands less.

## Type safety

- Always import row types from `@/payload-types`, never re-declare them.
- Cast block component props to the generated `OfferShowcaseBlock` etc., not `any` or `unknown`.

## Access control & hooks

- New collections default-restrict mutations to `authenticated`, reads to `authenticatedOrPublished`.
- For any collection rendered in `RenderBlocks`, add a `revalidate<Slug>` afterChange/afterDelete hook mirroring `revalidatePage`.

## Globals candidates

Site-wide content (CTA emails, social links, default "Pogadajmy" copy) belongs in a `SiteSettings` global, not duplicated across blocks.
